## 5.5 Module 5: Group Ride and Push-to-Talk

**Priority:** Medium  
**Release:** Later Phase

### Objective

Provide radio-style communication for organised riding groups.

### Group Ride Management

Organisers should be able to:

- Create a group ride.
- Define ride name, date and time.
- Add meeting and destination points.
- Invite riders.
- Generate QR codes.
- Generate joining codes.
- Send direct invitations.
- Assign ride marshals.
- View participants.

### Push-to-Talk Requirements

- Press-and-hold audio transmission.
- Real-time audio distribution.
- Group audio channels.
- Marshal announcements.
- Participant management.
- Connection status.
- Automatic reconnection.
- Mute functionality.
- Emergency communication channel.

### Connectivity Strategy

**Online PTT**

- Internet-based real-time audio.
- Central group communication service.
- Large group support.
- User authentication and channel permissions.

**Offline / Mesh PTT**

- Explore Wi-Fi Direct and Bluetooth.
- Device-to-device audio transmission.
- Communication relayed through participating devices.
- No dependency on central internet connectivity in supported configurations.

Offline communication requires a separate technical feasibility study covering range, interference, compatibility, battery consumption and network topology.

